{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGMS9dLzfMp5iBC6LCBC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled F1 **DISMISS refuted**. The verdict is committed as `f531b944c` in `docs/reviews/wi-958/009-ADJUDICATE-551aeb7.md`, with both required trailers.\n\n**What's real:** in an adopter repo, the review-owed marker would count as dirt.\n- The shipped `gitignore.template` doesn't ignore `out/review-owed`; this repo's own `.gitignore` ignores all of `out/`.\n- The attest step refuses a worktree holding any untracked file git doesn't ignore.\n- The draw gate and `attest_build` both record that refusal as a red.\n\nSo if `attest` ran next to the marker, it would record a red.\n\n**Why the stated scenario doesn't happen on any supported route:**\n- **The marker is only ever written over an attested tip.** Exit 9 fires only after review draws fail repeatedly. A draw happens only after the draw gate has found a verified attestation, or written one itself. A red at the gate drops the round, so exit 9 can't follow it.\n- **Nothing changes the tip before the resume.** The dispatcher parks an exit-9 lane untouched: no refresh, no merge. The failed draws commit only session logs and telemetry, which the attestation search steps over. So the resumed gate finds the attestation and never calls `attest`.\n- **\"Every later build stays red\" doesn't follow.** `complete_review_round` deletes the marker as its first act, for every verdict, before any rework build runs.\n\nThe reviewer's probe hand-built an unattested tip and placed the marker beside it. That's a state the kit's own routes never produce, which the review threat model excludes.\n\n**One rare residual path, recorded in the verdict:** the attestation search stops after 64 commits. A lane parked at exit 9 over many cycles of a total reviewer outage could pile up more than 64 record-only commits, after which the gate *would* run `attest` beside the marker. That fails closed, though: the lane hits its red cap and closes partial with its work kept. It's MINOR at most and not a convergence-class defect. Adding `out/review-owed` to the template is cheap hygiene the coordinator can take as a follow-up if it wants.\n\nAs before, the hook's `format` step was skipped because ruff isn't installed for its Python 3.12. I left the coordinator's `.requested` marker untracked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4103,"cache_read_input_tokens":584073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4103},"output_tokens":706,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"c8f4b3fe-a485-441c-8835-a3d288821155","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:46:53.107Z","request_id":"req_011CgGMS8rTjfGTJFFyRRiGT"}
